1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
On Sunday, August 2nd, there was an event by Liberal Friends of Israel at Central Shule, the intention being to meet candidates for the coming election.

2
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:18,120
The patrons were David Southwick, MP, Deputy Leader of the Victorian Liberal Party, Tim Wilson, Shadow Treasurer, and Senator James Paterson.

3
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:31,740
Candidates featured Rachel Westaway, Member for Prahran, Amelia Hamer, Candidate for Malvern, David Kitchen, Candidate for Bayswater, Frank Schiefler, Candidate for Hastings, and others.

4
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:44,480
Good evening everyone. My name is James Paterson, and on behalf of my fellow patrons of the Liberal Friends of Israel, David Southwick and Tim Wilson, it's my pleasure to welcome you all here this evening for tonight's events.

5
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:48,100
Can I thank President of the Shule, Phil Goldman, and the Rabbits.

6
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:50,360
Rabbi Shmuel, thank you so much for having us here.

7
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:54,460
I'll ask the Rabbi to say a prayer to open tonight's event in a moment.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,920
But I want to recognise some of the special guests and supporters that we have here tonight.

9
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:05,980
David will be interviewing our state candidates in a moment on the stage, and we'll introduce them when they join us.

10
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,240
But I also want to recognise other candidates who've joined us here tonight.

11
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:11,520
Max Williams, our candidate for Roeville.

12
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,780
Deirdre De Monte, our candidate for North East Metro Region.

13
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,340
And Theo Zografos, our candidate for Ashwood.

14
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:18,040
Thank you very much.

15
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,900
Thank you very much for joining us as well.

16
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:27,860
I also want to recognise Danny Lamb, our chair of the Liberal Friends of Israel, and he will have some words to say later.

17
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:33,240
And Helen Shardy, the former member for Caulfield and founder of the Liberal Friends of Israel.

18
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,540
Helen, so good to see you here.

19
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:45,960
Friends, in 17 weeks' time, on the 28th of November, Australia's foreign policy will not be on the ballot.

20
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,040
But.

21
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,400
Our community safety will be.

22
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:59,600
And the Andrews, Allen, and now Carroll governments have failed the Jewish community, and all Victorians, when it comes to community safety.

23
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:07,320
They allowed our CBD to become a no-go zone for Jews for two years.

24
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:17,300
They allowed propaganda, flags and symbols of Hamas, Hezbollah, Palestinian Islamic Jihad to be displayed on our streets openly,

25
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:19,900
without any consequences at all.

26
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,920
They allowed our schools to be graffitied.

27
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:32,240
This shul was shut down during Shabbat on the advice of the Victoria Police because they were concerned for the safety of the occupants inside.

28
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:36,640
And another shul, not far from here, was burnt to the ground.

29
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,480
This is a disgrace.

30
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:47,280
All Victorians, but particularly Jewish Victorians, are entitled to feel better, to have better, and to have better lives.

31
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,300
And they are entitled to the protection from their government in Victoria.

32
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:55,800
And if there is a change of government in November, if Jess Wilson is your next Premier, I guarantee you will.

33
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:00,680
David and the State Candidates have a bit more to say later about those community safety policies.

34
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:04,900
But really this is the most important election in Victoria's history.

35
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:11,060
At least in my short life, and I suspect in the somewhat longer lives of some of you in the audience here this evening.

36
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:17,280
So there will be an appeal at the end of tonight to do everything you can to support these outstanding State Candidates.

37
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,200
To make sure they win their seats.

38
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:20,840
We change this government.

39
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:23,360
And we give Victoria the fresh start that we need.

40
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:25,420
Rabbi, please lead us in prayer.

41
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:29,880
Thank you James.

42
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:36,660
I will recite the prayer.

43
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,680
But you can't ask a Rabbi to occupy a pulpit and not share a reflection.

44
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:41,460
So I will.

45
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,260
While this is absolutely a liberal friends of Israel case.

46
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:56,980
It is truly wonderful and a privilege for the President and myself to be able to open our doors and welcome you all here this evening for this event.

47
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:02,160
And it is fitting that we are sitting in a shul, in a sanctuary, in a synagogue.

48
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:07,200
A place where people come together and sit side by side and pray.

49
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,180
People from all backgrounds.

50
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,400
People from different persuasions.

51
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,940
People who even have different political views.

52
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:19,880
Yet sit side by side, united in a mission.

53
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,200
To be ambassadors of good.

54
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,240
To be ambassadors of light.

55
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,820
To be proud of who we are as Australians.

56
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:31,380
And proud of who we are supporters of our beloved Israel as well.

57
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:33,760
Represented by the flags in the room.

58
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,600
So my reflection this evening is this.

59
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:43,280
The particular part of the Torah that we read in the synagogue this week.

60
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:45,580
The name of which is Re'eh.

61
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:45,680
Re'eh.

62
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,300
Re'eh means to see.

63
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:50,620
What are we supposed to see?

64
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,440
We'll read the whole first verse.

65
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:55,380
It's the fourth part of the book of Yerushalayim.

66
00:04:55,740 --> 00:05:03,220
Re'eh anochi noten lifneichem hayom b'racha u'klala.

67
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:07,960
Which means, see, I am placed before you today.

68
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,660
Blessing and curse.

69
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:13,980
The Torah essentially is asking us.

70
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:17,100
To cultivate the ability to see.

71
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,480
To see with moral clarity.

72
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,000
To see with wisdom.

73
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,580
To see with vision.

74
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:28,540
And in an age where moral clarity is clouded, is obscured.

75
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:31,360
By noise, by misinformation, by ideology.

76
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:35,940
It is incumbent upon us to listen to that first word, Re'eh.

77
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:39,900
To be able to see with clear vision, with wisdom.

78
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,000
And those who hold public office.

79
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:43,820
The leaders among us.

80
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,720
And yes, we are all leaders in our own right.

81
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:47,220
Carry an extraordinary responsibility.

82
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,260
Because their words, their choices.

83
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,860
The things that they stand up proudly for.

84
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,720
Really genuinely impact our lives.

85
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,840
So my prayer this evening is that we should all be blessed.

86
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,580
With clarity, with wisdom, with vision.

87
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:07,420
Particularly those who hold public office and leadership position.

88
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:13,040
May the Almighty bless this beautiful country of Australia and all its good citizens.

89
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,900
May the Almighty bless our beautiful Israel.

90
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:18,480
Protect her citizens and her defenders.

91
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:21,440
And as we are going to read in this week's portion as well.

92
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:25,480
Israel should be able to dwell with its borders securely and safely.

93
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:28,240
Those who bless Israel shall be blessed.

94
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:31,740
Those who stand and advocate for her shall be blessed.

95
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:36,100
And this wonderful relationship between Australia and Israel.

96
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:39,400
Continue to flourish through the amazing work that has been done.

97
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,560
By people who are sitting here.

98
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:45,380
Who are sitting here in this room as well.

99
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,800
May we all be blessed.

100
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,880
Rabbi, thank you so much.

101
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:52,640
Now I want to hand over to my friend and colleague Tim Wilson.

102
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:56,460
Our shadow treasurer and the local member to many of you who live in Goldstone.

103
00:06:56,740 --> 00:07:01,960
But also someone who's stood very clearly with the Jewish community and with Israel.

104
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:07,180
If anybody was in any doubt about where Tim stood during the last federal election campaign.

105
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,540
He wanted to clear it up.

106
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,620
He took out an ad on the front page of the Jewish News.

107
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,820
Which just had two key words.

108
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,800
Proud Zionist.

109
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,760
Not everyone was willing to say that.

110
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:19,480
In Goldstone.

111
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:22,800
But Tim was.

112
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:26,020
And I know every one of you stands with him in being a proud Zionist too.

113
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:26,460
Tim.

114
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,100
Thank you.

115
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:32,740
Well thank you James so much for that kind introduction.

116
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:37,880
And can I also acknowledge of course my fellow co-patriots and liberal friends of Israel.

117
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,600
To the state candidates.

118
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:40,600
But to all of you.

119
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:46,640
I will concede that perhaps the words on that advertisement were slightly too short.

120
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,320
It should have said proud Zionist my whole adult life.

121
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:58,400
But it's important more than ever that we make tough choices in favour of our future.

122
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:01,980
And as James correctly outlined in a scarily.

123
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:07,480
Now we've got basically two hands and two feet's worth of weeks until the next state election.

124
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,580
And we've got to make a choice about the type of state we want.

125
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,260
And make no mistake.

126
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:17,000
That will feed into the type of nation we want to be.

127
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:20,280
And recently I gave a speech in the Federal Parliament.

128
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:24,800
The speech I gave talked about what a moral government is.

129
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:30,060
Because we all have our differences of opinion about a government and its decisions at different times.

130
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:33,140
The direction they take on economic or social policy.

131
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:37,760
But a moral government is one that makes decisions in the public interest.

132
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,060
Not in themselves.

133
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:42,340
Is guided by values and enhance the community.

134
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,900
Not simply enhance the interest of people of power.

135
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,660
And then I balanced that out.

136
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:51,540
Against the decisions of our federal governments.

137
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:54,040
And looking at the voice referendum.

138
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,560
Whatever your view on the specifics of that issue was.

139
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:01,580
That they put the social solidarity of our most marginalised population on a ballot paper.

140
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,920
Knowing it would fail.

141
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:06,100
And I don't believe that's a moral act of a moral government.

142
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,400
Certainly not moral leadership.

143
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:11,200
Then of course in the weeks leading up to the voice referendum.

144
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:14,240
We had the horrific events of October 7 overseas.

145
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:15,640
In Israel.

146
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,660
And more importantly.

147
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:20,780
The failure of leadership and moral clarity.

148
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,340
Exactly as the Rabbi outlined.

149
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:28,560
About the direction our country was going to go from that moment.

150
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:32,980
A spectacular failure of moral leadership and moral clarity.

151
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,540
That went from the Sydney Opera House.

152
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:36,740
And failing to condemn.

153
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:40,660
The target and demonisation of Australia's Jewish community.

154
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,160
To what we saw as we know.

155
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:47,580
Only just out the front here on the 10th of November a few weeks later.

156
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:52,340
To of course continued attacks on students and education.

157
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:55,860
And of course escalating all the way to the most horrific terrorist incident.

158
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,760
On our most famous beach.

159
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,480
And after that.

160
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:03,120
After the scale of the terror that has been enacted.

161
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:05,900
Not just on the Jewish community though it has been.

162
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:09,280
But in ripping the social fabric that divided our country.

163
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:12,460
The government after being dragged kicking and screaming.

164
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:14,700
Called a Royal Commission.

165
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,720
They fought against it every step of the way.

166
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:21,860
And one of the things I'm most proud of is the number of local residents.

167
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:25,040
Who have repented to paper and shared their voice.

168
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,720
And directly inputted into the Royal Commission.

169
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:30,240
I've done so the same.

170
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,900
Because one of the things we need is truth telling.

171
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,820
Sometimes you have to hold a mirror up to a country.

172
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:39,040
To show a sense of clarity about who we are.

173
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:43,400
To make sure that we can target the evil that sits amongst us.

174
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:47,520
Because there cannot be a nation where we continue to move forward together.

175
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:53,440
Where we tolerate the level of stigmatisation and demonisation of Australia's Jewish community.

176
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,420
It doesn't just go to the heart of the Jewish community.

177
00:10:55,580 --> 00:11:00,840
It goes to the very core and the social fabric of who we are as a people.

178
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:05,300
And I've seen my colleague Julia Lisa who's testified recently.

179
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,740
Before the Royal Commission.

180
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:09,180
And told a heartbreaking story.

181
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:14,080
About how he explains to his son his place in our country.

182
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:18,660
The sense of safety from so many people who have developed their own submissions.

183
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:21,240
Talking about the challenges that they have.

